// The demo site OG card. Built in Figma on the house OG template
// (section "OG images" 3124:8585, cloned from OG · botshield.ai 3124:8586)
// as "OG · demo.botshield.ai" 3312:3054.
//
// Exported at 2× — 2400×1260 — because 1200×630 went grainy on a retina
// timeline, and flattened to RGB: the card has nothing transparent, and an
// alpha channel is both wasted bytes and a thing some crawlers composite wrong.
//
// The phone is a live screenshot of /signup, so it goes stale when that page’s
// copy changes. It carried the retired "one account per human" line for one
// revision. When re-shooting: upload, then CHECK the fill actually moved — an
// upload can succeed and not be placed (no placedOnNodeId in the response),
// and the export then renders the old image with no error anywhere.
//
// Served at /og.png. Same pattern as the favicon: the bytes live in the worker,
// because this repo has no static asset pipeline.
export const OG_PNG_B64 = '';
